7. Do not globally break mouse navigation

Be careful with js/core/menu-navigator.js.

Other Alva screens intentionally use the global behavior where mouse hover can move menu focus.

Do not globally remove that behavior just to fix Quick Battle.

Make the change scoped.

A clean approach would be to introduce an explicit opt-out attribute/class for elements whose mouse hover is preview-only, for example something conceptually similar to:

data-nav-no-hover-focus

Then have the global pointer-over logic ignore only those elements.

The exact name is up to you, but the architecture should make the intent obvious.

The Quick Battle card can still remain a [data-nav] item for keyboard/gamepad navigation.

Mouse hover simply should not hijack DOM focus for this specific preview-only card.

